            <ArticleTitle>Effect of biphasic waveforms on transvenous defibrillation thresholds in patients with coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1098-100</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study is a prospective, randomized comparison of monophasic and biphasic defibrillation thresholds in 19 patients with a single transvenous lead. Despite using reverse polarity and optimal tilts for the monophasic waveform, the defibrillation threshold was reduced with biphasic shocks from 15.8 +/- 11.3 to 11.5 +/- 6.1 (p &lt;0.05) with comparable reductions of leading edge voltage and current.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
